<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Longitudinal Tabular Transformer</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tokenization.</span> Each feature is embedded independently into
<math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>: for continuous feature <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with value
<math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(k)}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(k)}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for categorical feature <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> at level <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(k)}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(k)}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>
from vocabulary <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{(k)}_{i,j}=x^{(k)}_{i,j}w_{k}+b_{k},\qquad u^{(k)}_{i,j}=E_{k}\bigl[c^{(k)}_{i,j}\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{(k)}_{i,j}=x^{(k)}_{i,j}w_{k}+b_{k},\qquad u^{(k)}_{i,j}=E_{k}\bigl[c^{(k)}_{i,j}\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k},b_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k},b_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V_{k}|\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V_{k}|\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Missingness is
represented explicitly rather than imputed: where the indicator
<math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{(k)}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{(k)}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is active a learned vector is added,
<math id="S3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{(k)}_{i,j}\!\leftarrow\!u^{(k)}_{i,j}+m^{(k)}_{i,j}\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{(k)}_{i,j}\!\leftarrow\!u^{(k)}_{i,j}+m^{(k)}_{i,j}\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. An absent
crew-assignment timestamp records that no crew has yet been assigned, so the
absence is itself informative. Stacking gives
<math id="S3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{F\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{F\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=p+q=54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=p+q=54</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intra-revision axis.</span> With <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TB}(A)=\tilde{A}+\mathrm{FFN}(\mathrm{LN}(\tilde{A}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TB</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>FFN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>LN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TB}(A)=\tilde{A}+\mathrm{FFN}(\mathrm{LN}(\tilde{A}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}=A+\mathrm{MHA}(\mathrm{LN}(A))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>MHA</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>LN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}=A+\mathrm{MHA}(\mathrm{LN}(A))</annotation></semantics></math>, and a
learned pooling token <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> prepended at index <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> so that
<math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(0)}_{i,j}=[\rho;U_{i,j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(0)}_{i,j}=[\rho;U_{i,j}]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U^{(\ell+1)}_{i,j}=\mathrm{TB}^{\mathrm{feat}}\bigl(U^{(\ell)}_{i,j}\bigr),\quad\ell=0,\dots,L_{f}-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>TB</mi><mi>feat</mi></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(\ell+1)}_{i,j}=\mathrm{TB}^{\mathrm{feat}}\bigl(U^{(\ell)}_{i,j}\bigr),\quad\ell=0,\dots,L_{f}-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i,j}=U^{(L_{f})}_{i,j}[0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i,j}=U^{(L_{f})}_{i,j}[0]</annotation></semantics></math>. Parameters are shared across positions and
events; joint attention over the <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\times F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\times F</annotation></semantics></math> grid needs <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(W^{2}F^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(W^{2}F^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise
terms against <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(WF^{2}+W^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(WF^{2}+W^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> factorised. Padded positions are zeroed and, by
(<a href="#S3.E9" title="In III Longitudinal Tabular Transformer ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), never attended.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temporal encoding.</span> Revisions arrive at irregular intervals set by
operational activity, so positional index alone is inadequate. We apply a
learned periodic representation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> to six channels
<math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\tau)_{n}=\begin{cases}\omega_{n}\tau+\varphi_{n},&amp;n=0,\\
\sin(\omega_{n}\tau+\varphi_{n}),&amp;1\leq n&lt;d_{t},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\tau)_{n}=\begin{cases}\omega_{n}\tau+\varphi_{n},&amp;n=0,\\
\sin(\omega_{n}\tau+\varphi_{n}),&amp;1\leq n&lt;d_{t},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\omega_{n},\varphi_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\omega_{n},\varphi_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> learned; the linear term preserves monotone elapsed
time, the periodic terms capture diurnal crew scheduling. Concatenating and
projecting gives <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i,j}=W_{\tau}[\phi(\tau^{(1)}_{i,j});\dots;\phi(\tau^{(6)}_{i,j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i,j}=W_{\tau}[\phi(\tau^{(1)}_{i,j});\dots;\phi(\tau^{(6)}_{i,j})]</annotation></semantics></math>. Channels are elapsed time since the outage opened,
since the previous revision, hour of day, time since storm onset, a causal
proxy for storm peak, and normalised window position; the peak proxy uses the
running maximum of customers interrupted to <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the realised peak
being unobservable at prediction time.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Static, context, and inter-revision axes.</span> Static features are
tokenized as in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In III Longitudinal Tabular Transformer ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and mean-pooled to <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, prepended
rather than broadcast, since replicating a constant across <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> positions
consumes attention capacity without conveying information. Context is
projected per position into <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{W\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{W\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sequence</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(0)}_{i,j}=\bigl[\sigma_{i};\,h_{i,j-W+1}+\pi_{i,j-W+1};\dots;h_{i,j}+\pi_{i,j}\bigr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(0)}_{i,j}=\bigl[\sigma_{i};\,h_{i,j-W+1}+\pi_{i,j-W+1};\dots;h_{i,j}+\pi_{i,j}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">in <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{(W+1)\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{(W+1)\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, indexed <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,\dots,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,\dots,W</annotation></semantics></math>, receives one
cross-attention layer against the context, <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(0)}\!\leftarrow\!H^{(0)}+\mathrm{MHA}(\mathrm{LN}(H^{(0)}),G,G;M^{\mathrm{ctx}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>MHA</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>LN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>ctx</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(0)}\!\leftarrow\!H^{(0)}+\mathrm{MHA}(\mathrm{LN}(H^{(0)}),G,G;M^{\mathrm{ctx}})</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H^{(\ell+1)}_{i,j}=\mathrm{TB}^{\mathrm{rev}}\bigl(H^{(\ell)}_{i,j},M\bigr),\quad\ell=0,\dots,L_{r}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>TB</mi><mi>rev</mi></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\ell+1)}_{i,j}=\mathrm{TB}^{\mathrm{rev}}\bigl(H^{(\ell)}_{i,j},M\bigr),\quad\ell=0,\dots,L_{r}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The always-present static token extends (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In II Problem Formulation ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) by <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{m}_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{m}_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{m}_{a}=m^{\mathrm{obs}}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{m}_{a}=m^{\mathrm{obs}}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq a\leq W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq a\leq W</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{ab}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;\tilde{m}_{b}=1\\
-\infty,&amp;\text{else}\end{cases}\qquad M^{\mathrm{ctx}}_{ab}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;m^{\mathrm{obs}}_{b}=1\\
-\infty,&amp;\text{else,}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>else</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>ctx</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>else,</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{ab}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;\tilde{m}_{b}=1\\
-\infty,&amp;\text{else}\end{cases}\qquad M^{\mathrm{ctx}}_{ab}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;m^{\mathrm{obs}}_{b}=1\\
-\infty,&amp;\text{else,}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbb{R}^{(W+1)\times(W+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbb{R}^{(W+1)\times(W+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\mathrm{ctx}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(W+1)\times W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>ctx</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\mathrm{ctx}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(W+1)\times W}</annotation></semantics></math>, added to the logits before the softmax. Both
depend only on the key index <math id="S3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> and are key-padding masks, not general
attention patterns.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Absence of temporal leakage)<span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">No causal mask is required. Every position of <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> indexes
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}\leq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}\leq j</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i,j^{\prime}}\leq t_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i,j^{\prime}}\leq t_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,j^{\prime}}\in\Omega_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,j^{\prime}}\in\Omega_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the information available at <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>; so
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a measurable function of <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> irrespective of the
attention pattern applied within the window. Bidirectional attention is
therefore admissible and strictly more expressive. This does not hold for the
alternative in which one pass over an entire event is supervised at every
position, which does require causal masking.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Head.</span> With <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}=\psi(H^{(L_{r})}_{i,j}[W])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}=\psi(H^{(L_{r})}_{i,j}[W])</annotation></semantics></math> we predict ordered
levels <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\{\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2},\kappa_{3}\}=\{\tfrac{1}{2},\tfrac{5}{6},\tfrac{9}{10}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\{\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2},\kappa_{3}\}=\{\tfrac{1}{2},\tfrac{5}{6},\tfrac{9}{10}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
as a base plus non-negative increments,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{1})}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{1})}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s\cdot\mathrm{softplus}\bigl(a_{1}^{\top}v_{i,j}+b_{1}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>softplus</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s\cdot\mathrm{softplus}\bigl(a_{1}^{\top}v_{i,j}+b_{1}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{m})}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{m})}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{m-1})}_{i,j}+s\cdot\mathrm{softplus}\bigl(a_{m}^{\top}v_{i,j}+b_{m}\bigr),\;m=2,3." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>softplus</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{m-1})}_{i,j}+s\cdot\mathrm{softplus}\bigl(a_{m}^{\top}v_{i,j}+b_{m}\bigr),\;m=2,3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Non-negativity follows from the softplus and monotonicity
<math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{1})}\!\leq\!\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{2})}\!\leq\!\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{3})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{1})}\!\leq\!\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{2})}\!\leq\!\hat{y}^{(\kappa_{3})}</annotation></semantics></math>
from non-negativity of each increment, so the ordered levels cannot cross for
any input. The published estimate uses <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\star}=\kappa_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\star}=\kappa_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; the other
heads provide lower and upper operational levels trained with pinball losses. The axes cost <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L_{f}WF^{2}d)+O(L_{r}W^{2}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L_{f}WF^{2}d)+O(L_{r}W^{2}d)</annotation></semantics></math> per
sample; with <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=54</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}=4</annotation></semantics></math> the feature axis exceeds the
sequence axis by about <math id="S3.p5.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="73\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>73</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">73\times</annotation></semantics></math> and dominates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Objective</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Internal customer outage survey analysis indicates that satisfaction responds
asymmetrically to error: underprediction, where restoration arrives later than
promised, reduces satisfaction sharply; overprediction is tolerated to a
threshold and penalised beyond. We encode that operational preference through
the following piecewise penalty template, with <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\hat{y}-y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\hat{y}-y</annotation></semantics></math> in hours:</p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\epsilon)=\begin{cases}\alpha|\epsilon|,&amp;\epsilon&lt;0,\\
|\epsilon|,&amp;0\leq\epsilon\leq\theta,\\
\beta|\epsilon|,&amp;\epsilon&gt;\theta,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\epsilon)=\begin{cases}\alpha|\epsilon|,&amp;\epsilon&lt;0,\\
|\epsilon|,&amp;0\leq\epsilon\leq\theta,\\
\beta|\epsilon|,&amp;\epsilon&gt;\theta,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=8</annotation></semantics></math> h, <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=2</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from internal
customer outage survey analysis rather than tuned to model performance, and
held fixed for every method compared.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\star}=\alpha/(\alpha+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\star}=\alpha/(\alpha+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho_{\kappa}(u)=u(\kappa-\mathbb{I}[u&lt;0])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\kappa}(u)=u(\kappa-\mathbb{I}[u&lt;0])</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=y-\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=y-\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Restricted to <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\epsilon|\leq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\epsilon|\leq\theta</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#S4.E12" title="In IV Objective ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) equals <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha+1)</annotation></semantics></math> times the pinball loss at <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique level for which (<a href="#S4.E12" title="In IV Objective ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) and
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> are proportional on that region.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Both losses are positively homogeneous and piecewise linear in <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
with a single kink at <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so proportionality on
<math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\epsilon|\leq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\epsilon|\leq\theta</annotation></semantics></math> holds iff the ratio of branch slopes agrees. For
<math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=-\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=-\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\kappa}(u)=\kappa|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\kappa}(u)=\kappa|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\epsilon)=\alpha|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\epsilon)=\alpha|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math>; for <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\epsilon\leq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\epsilon\leq\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\kappa}(u)=(1-\kappa)|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\kappa}(u)=(1-\kappa)|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\epsilon)=|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\epsilon)=|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math>. The
slope ratio of <math id="S4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa/(1-\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa/(1-\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and that of <math id="S4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>; these agree exactly when <math id="S4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\alpha/(\alpha+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\alpha/(\alpha+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
uniqueness. Substituting <math id="S4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> yields
<math id="S4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\kappa^{\star}}(u)=\alpha(\alpha+1)^{-1}|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\kappa^{\star}}(u)=\alpha(\alpha+1)^{-1}|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math> against
<math id="S4.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math> on the first branch and <math id="S4.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha+1)^{-1}|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha+1)^{-1}|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math>
against <math id="S4.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\epsilon|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\epsilon|</annotation></semantics></math> on the second; the constant is <math id="S4.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha+1</annotation></semantics></math> on both.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=5</annotation></semantics></math>, the slope ratio within the central operating region
corresponds exactly to <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\star}=5/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\star}=5/6</annotation></semantics></math>, motivating the primary level of
(<a href="#S3.E11" title="In III Longitudinal Tabular Transformer ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). We retain the fractional representation so this local
correspondence holds without approximation. The resulting operating point
intentionally penalises underprediction more heavily than moderate
overprediction and therefore should not be interpreted as a
conditional-mean estimate.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Smoothing and training.</span> Equation (<a href="#S4.E12" title="In IV Objective ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is an operational
penalty template with breakpoints at <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\{0,\theta\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\{0,\theta\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Training
uses its Huber-smoothed surrogate <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, which preserves the outer
linear branches and uses quadratic transitions within
<math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-neighbourhoods of the breakpoints, with <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.25</annotation></semantics></math> h. We write
<math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\delta,\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\delta,\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> for the identically smoothed pinball loss. The same <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is used for every
method, including the boosting baselines, whose Newton updates need a
non-vanishing second derivative. A stability term
<math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\mathrm{stab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>stab</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\mathrm{stab}}</annotation></semantics></math> penalises movement of the published timestamp
between consecutive revisions beyond <math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{tol}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>tol</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{tol}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> h, computed
under an event-grouped sampler. With
<math id="S4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\kappa)}_{i,j}=\hat{y}^{(\kappa)}_{i,j}-y_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\kappa)}_{i,j}=\hat{y}^{(\kappa)}_{i,j}-y_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{|S|}\!\!\sum_{(i,j)\in S}\!\!\Bigl[\ell_{\delta}\bigl(\epsilon^{(\kappa^{\star})}_{i,j}\bigr)+\lambda_{q}\!\!\!\!\sum_{\kappa\in Q\setminus\{\kappa^{\star}\}}\!\!\!\!\rho_{\delta,\kappa}\bigl(y_{i,j}-\hat{y}^{(\kappa)}_{i,j}\bigr)\Bigr]+\lambda\mathcal{L}^{\mathrm{stab}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>stab</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{|S|}\!\!\sum_{(i,j)\in S}\!\!\Bigl[\ell_{\delta}\bigl(\epsilon^{(\kappa^{\star})}_{i,j}\bigr)+\lambda_{q}\!\!\!\!\sum_{\kappa\in Q\setminus\{\kappa^{\star}\}}\!\!\!\!\rho_{\delta,\kappa}\bigl(y_{i,j}-\hat{y}^{(\kappa)}_{i,j}\bigr)\Bigr]+\lambda\mathcal{L}^{\mathrm{stab}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Outside the smoothing neighbourhoods, <math id="S4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> retains the linear
branches of (<a href="#S4.E12" title="In IV Objective ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>); within them the quadratic transitions preserve
a nonzero penalty for systematic conservatism. The objective therefore has no
flat region.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scale.</span> The breakpoints of (<a href="#S4.E12" title="In IV Objective ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) are in hours; a monotone
transform such as <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+y)</annotation></semantics></math> would displace them to input-dependent
locations and destroy that interpretation, so we supervise on the hour scale.
The heavy tail is accommodated by linearity of <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> outside the smoothing
neighbourhoods and by the constant <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In III Longitudinal Tabular Transformer ‣ Predicting Estimated Times of Restoration for Electrical Outages Using Longitudinal Tabular Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), set to the
training-partition median remaining time per company so softplus arguments
are <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> at initialisation. Inputs are scaled by median and IQR on training
storms only. Configuration: <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=128</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}=4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> heads, one context
cross-attention layer, <math id="S4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}=16</annotation></semantics></math>, dropout <math id="S4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, AdamW (decay <math id="S4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), lr
<math id="S4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> cosine with <math id="S4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math>-step warmup, batch <math id="S4.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math> M parameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Five-seed test means by operating company, ordered by median revisions per outage and weighted by customer-hours
